From 2b0e1835eb4eb6599a465d49a1bb0fb52e46f448 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 01:13:05 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] API 36 (FORK-10 a): mod-defined living entities: entity_kind
 content, spawn-mod-entity, entities-tick, saved with the world

Kinds are declared in data/<id>/horizon/entity_kind/*.json. The game keeps each entity's state (saved bytes, container slots, energy, skin, name) in data/horizon/mod_entities.json, spawns it for the mod (spawn-mod-entity answers with a ticket as spawn-mob does), asks the mods for registration.mod-entities each tick (entities-tick) and removes it on remove-entity or an update's remove. Server side only: clients do not see it yet.
Also: the menu text constants live in content (the content-only build compiled without them), and the bow hooks are cfg(mods).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01RYe92n7spgy8vtm4CovRWA
